    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35780" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐννεάζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spend one's youth in,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγέθει σώματος ἐννεάσαι</span>
			<i>to be of</i> great stature <i>in one's youth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				2.54
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ τῶν πραγμάτων ἀκριβεστέρᾳ
					καταλήψει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.622
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. [τῇ βασιλείᾳ] καὶ
				ἐγγηράσκει,</span> of one crowned in his mother's womb,
				<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				4.25
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόδον ἐννεάσαν τῷ ἦρι</span>
			<i>having bloomed</i> in spring, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				51
			</span></i>.</div>
